      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum.\n\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). The FDA label lists 2,550 mg/day as the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
